! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F202A sub-tests 19 and 20
! (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.33, octal 011422.00-011432.40) --
! the first block of the FP diagnostic RUN on this model (previously
! only its BB lines and sign-modifier loads were checked as encodings).
!
! Each sub-test loads FPK2 (unnormalized), zeroes the indicators, and
! COMPARES it (K, unnormalized) against another constant; the listing's
! own comment states the expected result -- "XFN RNG FRACT + AL ON",
! i.e. the arithmetic-low indicator AL must come on and AE/AH must be
! off. It then checks that with three SIC-prefixed branch-on-indicator
! instructions, each branching to the error routine SERS if the result
! is wrong:
!   SIC,SEN / BZAL,SERS   -- error if AL is OFF (branch on zero AL)
!   SIC,SEN / BAE,SERS     -- error if AE is ON
!   SIC,SEN / BAH,SERS     -- error if AH is ON
! A19 compares FPK2 vs FPK26, A20 compares FPK2 vs FPK21; both expect
! AL on. So a correct FP compare falls straight through both sub-tests
! to F202A21's location, where this transcription substitutes a PASS
! halt (BEW,$); any wrong indicator branches to SERS, where a FAIL halt
! sits. PC alone therefore says pass (halted at PASS) or fail (halted
! at SERS), the same self-checking mechanism the I-Box SIC-CB block uses.
!
! Substitutions (the SSIP diagnostic framework, all OUTSIDE the
! transcribed code range, given at their listed low-memory addresses so
! the SIC/branch machine code still matches the listing):
!   SERS (octal 1304) -> BEW,$   the error routine, replaced by a halt
!   SEN  (octal 1310) -> a scratch word the SIC stores the IC into
!   PASS (octal 11433, where F202A21 begins) -> BEW,$
! Constants FPK2/FPK21/FPK26 are transcribed from the pool on p.176 at
! their listed addresses (octal 22007/22032/22037), as the raw 64-bit
! floating-point words the diagnostic defines with %8=DD%BU=.
!
! Instructions used: L(U), Z, K(U), SIC, BZAL/BAE/BAH (branch on
! indicator), BEW -- all implemented. This block is the first to run a
! real FP compare against the diagnostic's own operands and check the
! AL/AE/AH indicators against IBM's stated expectation. The SIC pairs
! are full words landing at octal .40 (an odd half-word), exercising the
! half-word-aligned full-word instruction placement fixed this session
! (strap/README.md Gotchas item 19). verify_fp_compare_listing.py checks
! every transcribed half-word against the page's printed machine code.
!
! Observed: the model halts at PASS -- both compares (FPK2 vs FPK26,
! XFP range; FPK2 vs FPK21, N range) set exactly AL, so the single-
! precision FP compare handles these extreme-exponent operands as IBM's
! own diagnostic expects. Injection (AL and AH swapped in
! StretchExecute's FP compare arm): the model halts at SERS (PC 1416),
! the FAIL routine, exactly as predicted -- FPK2<FPK26 then set AH, so
! BZAL,SERS branched on AL being off. Reversed by the exact inverse
! edit (AGENTS.md rule 2); PASS restored.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes, at their real listed addresses --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $              ! error routine -> FAIL halt
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0      ! SIC stores the instruction counter here

! -- floating-point constants (pool, p.176) --
        SLC, (8)22007.0
FPK2    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777777777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22032.0
FPK21   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031177777777777777767
        SLC, (8)22037.0
FPK26   DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777577777777777777760

! -- the transcribed code (verbatim, at the listing's own addresses) --
        SLC, (8)11422.0
F202A19 L(U), FPK2          ! XFN RNG  FRACT +   AL ON
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FPK26         ! XFP RANGE, FRACT.+
        SIC, SEN
        BZAL, SERS          ! error if AL off and AE or AH on
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAH, SERS
F202A20 L(U), FPK2          ! XFN RNG  FRACT +   AL ON
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FPK21         ! N RANGE, FRACT.+
        SIC, SEN
        BZAL, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAH, SERS

! -- PASS halt where F202A21 begins --
        SLC, (8)11433.0
PASS    BEW, $              ! all AL-on checks fell through: success

        END, F202A19
